<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila biarmipes Turing wavelength at 1.5 µm (detail s0, 0 Ma) (Drosophila biarmipes)",
        "Drosophila biarmipes Turing wavelength at 1.5 µm (detail s0, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila biarmipes morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila biarmipes specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-biarmipes-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila biarmipes" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That the gallery plate is a micrograph of a 1.5 µm melanin lattice.",
        "does_not_claim: That the saturated lattice wavelength equals the linear lambda_c.",
        "does_not_claim: That yellow transcription is Schnakenberg kinetics.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 96² centroid 1.259 µm and 128² centroid 1.358 µm on the same 17.832 µm patch.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Ananassae subcritical and bipectinata shorter-wavelength shifts at fixed diffusivities.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg (a, b, D_u, D_v) whose linear lambda_c equals 1.486 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Gompel et al. 2005: D. biarmipes males deploy a novel yellow wing-spot enhancer.",
        "reported_in_source: Prud'homme et al. 2006: wing spots evolved repeatedly via yellow cis-regulatory elements.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator.",
        "transfer_boundary: 1.5 µm is the Delphi 3_subcellular_um assignment, not a length reported by Gompel.",
        "transfer_boundary: Chronoseries neighbors are catalog positions, not a phylogenetic ancestor chain." ;
